<title>UK: Novorossiisk pipelines closed for repair-source.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk pipelines closed for repair-source.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crude oil pipelines feeding Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea closed on Thursday for 60 hours of repair, a shipping source said on Friday.</p>
<p>The closure had not hindered the loading of Russian Export Blend onto the tanker Kriti Wave. The Biruinta is alongside and expected to depart in mid-afternoon.</p>
<p>The pipelines should be restored by the time of the arrival of the next vessel, the Agip Marche, on Saturday, the source said.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea and Baltic ports were working normally. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
